abstract: "AIDRIN (AI Data Readiness Infrastructure) is an open-source framework for assessing whether a dataset is ready for AI, remediating data if there are any issues, and transforming data to how it is needed by AI applications. AIDRIN evaluates data using a comprehensive set of dimensions, i.e., quality, structure, fairness and bias, feature importance, privacy and governance risk, and metadata usability. The framework also allows user-defined AI application-specific custom evaluation. It generates a report across these dimensions with visualizations, machine-readable JSON, and suggested remedies for the issues it finds. Users can also use the framework for performing custom remedies, and incorporate domain-specific knowledge so that assessments reflect the requirements of their field. AIDRIN can be used from a browser dashboard, the command line, a Python library, or an MCP server for agentic clients, and can run remotely on datasets that stay in place."
